he western way of life and i would say  this western model  of structure in the state we still  strongly connected and attached to the  grassroots and so we need there's a  choice to be made here either  we  we adopt this this model and we have to  improve certain indicators or we only be  africans and we have to  find a different way of certain things  mr pereira i want to talk to you about  the other big problem  guinea bissau has been dubbed a narco  state because of the rampant cocaine  trafficking through the country  how much is this contributing to the  political instability there  narcotraffic is not  a guinean phenomenon  and  the difference  between what we had in the past and what  we're having now  is  the willingness of the authorities to  work with the  international agencies to combat this  phenomenon either you are opening open  to cooperation or you close  the sovereignty and you claimed  not to cover it  just just to get some clarity there am i  hearing you say that  the the narco state  label is no longer applicable are you  saying uh cocaine trafficking is not as  bad  um because the government is is is  clamping down with the help of  international agencies  no i'm not saying none of those i'm  saying that we are not a norcal state  we have been labeled that because of  prevailing  of  officials that are connected to that  and i believe that to make a difference  is not just a question of the  willingness to fight it right but the  willingness to be open to cooperate with  international uh agencies that have the  capacity and also the structure to help  us impacting that phenomenon  and that was domingo simoes pereira a  politician and opposition leader in  guinea-bissau
 

